{"id": "EUVD-2026-103726", "enisaUuid": "7b328fd5-3b98-344a-80dc-eb40af6444c7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: ena: fix MMIO read buffer leak on probe failure\n\nena_device_init() initializes the MMIO read mechanism with\nena_com_mmio_reg_read_request_init(), which allocates a coherent DMA\nbuffer for MMIO read responses.\n\nThe normal removal path releases this buffer through\nena_com_mmio_reg_read_request_destroy(). However, if ena_probe() fails\nafter ena_device_init() succeeds, the error path destroys the admin\nresources and eventually frees ena_dev without destroying the MMIO read\nrequest, leaving the coherent DMA buffer allocated.\n\nCall ena_com_mmio_reg_read_request_destroy() in the probe error path\nbefore releasing the remaining device resources.\n\nThis issue was found by manual code inspection.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:16:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:12", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a0f5fd7a285f44fa402242f26feddfe1d4a0fc6c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7bd3e9a2d0c288e54f51df260d9433163f5fbc1e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/30ff01b4c7e419bb70f40f01dcd7f6af680808b3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/47785f9f638b064ce6e32e8e3b6f1ffd83849fc2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9476b4468862927297c94c440863cd8ed1e7cc83"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vj8m-9pww-pf2j", "CVE-2026-98486"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "067550b1-521a-3ba7-bae3-91b5e3e60ed7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1738cd3ed342294360d6a74d4e58800004bff854 <47785f9f638b064ce6e32e8e3b6f1ffd83849fc2"}, {"id": "1a0cbef6-0759-3e50-9fcb-6c7671aa9c65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1738cd3ed342294360d6a74d4e58800004bff854 <7bd3e9a2d0c288e54f51df260d9433163f5fbc1e"}, {"id": "44868f4e-e3c0-366c-b0ba-4c21dcfabaf1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "5f7ff5cf-e627-3764-9755-a503024375e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1738cd3ed342294360d6a74d4e58800004bff854 <30ff01b4c7e419bb70f40f01dcd7f6af680808b3"}, {"id": "6a34cff9-4625-3bbd-a203-725e2c20d703", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "7007c402-ec76-3e46-8f1e-d4922feb1241", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1738cd3ed342294360d6a74d4e58800004bff854 <9476b4468862927297c94c440863cd8ed1e7cc83"}, {"id": "80bbfcca-8646-3a14-b3b8-e1311a88e330", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "9b7b84d5-fb51-3486-acbd-d8e92034635b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1738cd3ed342294360d6a74d4e58800004bff854 <a0f5fd7a285f44fa402242f26feddfe1d4a0fc6c"}, {"id": "9ed7bd2e-837e-30c7-b53e-1c7b447ad079", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "b02055d7-190e-33dd-8179-b2a6b0a6884d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "cc141b34-f91e-30c9-91df-bb2144c496ad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.9"}, {"id": "dd331b9d-b8e2-36eb-b030-1a4d8f187131", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e39bc6a7-57d8-3c98-ae72-cfbfce96eaba", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}